        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: complete deterministic guarded-open reviews",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- complete exact-item reviews when apply returns one of five deterministic remain-open guards and the captured record agrees\n- emit guarded completion only when the candidate remains the final authoritative four-file tuple\n- suppress stale verdict routing for guarded results and requeue changed revisions or publish-race losers\n\n## Why\n\nStable apply guards were already writing the correct open state, but the publisher required comment-sync or terminal proof. Those jobs therefore retried indefinitely instead of completing. This keeps the completion path narrow and deterministic while preserving retries for transient or stale reviews.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `pnpm run build:all`\n- `node --test test/repair/event-apply-proof.test.ts test/repair/event-record-store.test.ts test/repair/git-publish.test.ts test/sweep-workflow.test.ts` (100 passed)\n- `pnpm run lint:repair`\n- `pnpm run lint:scripts`\n- targeted `oxfmt --check`\n- GPT-5.6 Sol High autoreview: clean, no accepted/actionable findings\n",
